mission "The Fleet at the Blue Line"
    name "The Fleet at the Blue Line"
    description "Protect the survey ships from a squadron that has mistaken their lantern code for a treasure signal."
    source "Pelican's Rest"
    destination "Stormhaven"
    reward 1590
    speaker offer "Admiral Horatio Vale"
    speaker visit "Admiral Horatio Vale"
    speaker complete "Admiral Horatio Vale"
    to offer
        has "The Drowned Crown Coordinates: done"
    objective kills 2
    battlefield "The Blue Line" 15100 6100
    enemy "Vale's Vanguard"
    enemy "Vale's Second"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Protect the survey ships from a squadron that has mistaken their lantern code for a treasure signal.`
            `Admiral Horatio Vale studies you for a moment. "The old sea charter settled one war, but it did not settle the past. The lost expedition sailed west under a sealed order, and its wake is stirring every ambitious captain in these waters."
            choice
                `(I will help uncover what happened.)`
                    accept
                `(Tell me what you are not saying.)`
                    goto details
                `(I have no wish to be drawn into another quarrel.)`
                    close
            label details
                `Admiral Horatio Vale lowers their voice. "The maps were altered, the convoy erased from the books, and someone has been buying witnesses. Follow the evidence, not the flags."`
                choice
                    `(Then I will take the matter in hand.)`
                        accept
                    `(Not today.)`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Fleet at the Blue Line. Protect the survey ships from a squadron that has mistaken their lantern code for a treasure signal."
    on visit
        conversation
            `Admiral Horatio Vale receives you at Stormhaven. The evidence fits another piece into the puzzle: the expedition was not searching for gold alone, but for a place deliberately removed from every official chart.`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Admiral Horatio Vale thanks you. "Every answer makes the sea less simple, captain. Yet the truth belongs to the people who live here, not to the first crown or company that can put a seal upon it."`
        log "Completed The Fleet at the Blue Line. Received 1590 gold. Protect the survey ships from a squadron that has mistaken their lantern code for a treasure signal."
